A||||14||Formula||Aftermarket Wheels.....(jedi mind trick), "You have to read this"||||3||
Z||000000||Formula||08-29-2000||08:55 PM||||who has purchased wheels for their fiero?<P>questions......<P>1.how much were they?<BR>2.what size?<BR>3.do you like them?<BR>4.do they talk to you?<P>I'm looking into getting some polished 5 stars that are the same size as my formula wheels (so I can use my new tires).  Anyone know of any cheap ones and/or does anyone know of any cheap wheels in general in 15x6 front and 15x7 rear.  I think the Z-Racing version of Enkei Zokus would look good on a fiero.  I think I saw them on a red coupe with all the moldings painted to match.  Anyone have any pics of that car (I saw it on here) I remember it had a roll cage too, but I cant seem to find it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Formula_sig.gif"> ||||reg||3
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||08-29-2000||10:08 PM||||My answers to the questions:<P>1. I got them way back in 93 so I don't really remember. I think that wheels and tires came to around $900.<P>2. They are 16x8 (I think, they may be 16x7)Image "Eclipse" (similar to Coddington's Ninja excpet no center hex nut cover and wearing some "Don't sue me" Black paint.) wearing 225/50 BFGoodrich Comp TA VR-4s.<P>3. I love that since they probably got sued for making them so close to Coddington's wheels I NEVER see them on another Fiero. Hell I don't see them at all, anywhere!<P>4. They talk to me all the time. When they aren't screaming "CLEAN US YOU DORK!" (Cross drilled rotors can be brutal with dust.) I see them smiling at me from across the parking lot (while Im walking to them)and they are saying, "Hey big boy, lets get into some trouble."  <P>Me love my Fiero? <P>Yeah.||||reg||6
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||08-29-2000||11:19 PM||||Mine are 17"x7" with 215/40ZR17 tires. They were 40mm or 42mm offset. They wanted $1400.00 but I paid $1009.00 them at Discount Tire Direct. I didnt like the center cap (picutred) so I went back and they gave me a new set of brushed alum. ones for free.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/019_18_1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/016_15.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycarsig.jpg">   <B>My 1985 2M4 Sport Coupe </B><P><BR><B>My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A></B><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 08-29-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000003||Philphine||08-30-2000||02:04 AM||||16x7.5 panther 106's (3 stars). 225/50- 16 front. 255/50-16 rear.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChadMan||08-30-2000||08:33 AM||||Haze, your wheels are keen (50's), far out (60's), groovy (70's), sweet (80's), and phat (90's).<P>But it looks like you live in an apartment/condo type situation.  Aren't you afraid some a$$hole will steal them?  (Maybe I'm just paranoid after getting my Fieros egged last year.)||||reg||9
Z||000005||HugGRRRFiero||08-30-2000||10:13 AM||||Formula, Discount Tire has pretty reasonable deals and handle a wide variety and brands of 15" wheels that your tires should fit.<P>The one's on my Fiero are 17"x7-1/2 MSR 132's, MSR I believe is a division of Eagle Alloys.  Don't they look like Enkei Zoku's?, check <A HREF="http://www.Enkei.com" TARGET=_blank>www.Enkei.com</A> under the Tuner wheels and compare to the pictures I posted of mine.<P>I liked the Zoku's too, but cost $289.99 a pop  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">, I stumbled across these looking thru an MSR brocure I picked up searching for wheels.  They are VERY similar and a bit cheaper.  Well, cheaper compared to the Zoku's.  I'm probably going to see more Fieros with these wheels now, but awe well.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">    <BR>    <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> <p>[This message has been edited by HugGRRRFiero (edited 08-30-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000006||Songman||08-30-2000||10:32 AM||||My wheels are 15x7 polished stars by a company called Platinum. Not sure who the parent company is. I am running 225/50x15s all the way around. All that meat really sets this little white 4-banger coupe off!<BR>The tires were about $95 each and the wheels were around $125 each. Of course, you have to pay all those extra charges, but they look great! I'll try to get a photo soon.||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||08-30-2000||11:47 AM||||17x7 x 2  17x8 x 2  Konig GT-R purchased in January of 99. cost with tires from <A HREF="http://www.discounttiredirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.discounttiredirect.com</A>  including shipping $1070. Yokohama A520 215-40 & 2 255x40. Loverd every minute of them... but they were REALLY heavey and the guys that tune my car made me sell them.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/travis.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Haze_Performance||08-31-2000||03:21 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ChadMan:<BR><B>Haze, your wheels are keen (50's), far out (60's), groovy (70's), sweet (80's), and phat (90's).<P>But it looks like you live in an apartment/condo type situation.  Aren't you afraid some a$$hole will steal them?  (Maybe I'm just paranoid after getting my Fieros egged last year.)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Thanks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>As for someone stealing them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> . I live in a very well protected suburb.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> The car has a $700+ Alarm, Every wheel has a lock, My neighbor is a State Trooper, The car stays the garage at night and if that wont do it..... I have a 9mm (1 clip has blanks the other one does NOT) that I can shoot over there head  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I just hope if it came to the last one, I grab the right clip  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycarsig.jpg">  <B>My 1985 2M4 Sport Coupe </B><P><BR><B>My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A></B>||||reg||12
Z||000009||Pontiaddict||08-31-2000||05:07 PM||||I have some old BBS wheels that came with the car. The guy I bought them from said they cost $200 a piece when he got them in 1991. They are 15x7 and have stock sized tires on them.<P>This won't help you since they don't make them anymore and I can't find any info on them. If anyone can ID them, I'd like to know.<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=990774&a=7280777&p=24718609&Sequence=1"> <BR> If this actually works.||||reg||1
Z||000010||StuGood||09-02-2000||02:12 PM||||9mm - ?  State trooper - ?  That's it - I'm no longer thinking of pilfering that nice $700 alarm system.<P>Oops.  Did I just type that out loud?||||reg||12
