Z||000012||Haze_Performance||09-02-2000||09:16 PM||||Cliff,<BR>Do you know what the name of those wheels?? <P>They look like "Elite Vipers".<BR>A buddy had a set on his Corvette.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycarsig.jpg">  <B>My 1985 2M4 Sport Coupe </B><P><BR><B>My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A></B>||||reg||10
Z||000013||Patrick's Dad||09-02-2000||09:18 PM||||Hmm... Cliff lives in Harlem.... That explains his Fiero's wheels....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I've always been partial to 5 spokes, but have been looking hard at the BBS RK or RKII, which, I guess, are modified 5 spokes... You gotta A) reduce unsprung weight for better suspension control, and B) Show off the cool 4 piston calipers and cross drilled rotors. My take is that I'd get them in 16x7 and 16x8 size, because I'd be afraid of my 17" rims making contact with the pavement on these New England roads. Plus, the harsh ride argument almost cancels out the 12" rotors argument....||||reg||12
